Determine the outcome of this case. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {6, 1, 5, 2, 2};
int acc = a[0];
for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > acc) acc = a[i];
return acc;

This item tests your reasoning. What does this string routine return?
String s = "ebbzy";
StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();
for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) out.append(s.charAt(i));
return out.toString();

Take a moment to solve this. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {0, 1, 5, 6, 10, 12};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 0) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 0) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Analyze the scenario presented. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(35);
Node b = new Node(15);
Node c = new Node(5);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Analyze the given configuration. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {4, 7, 9, 11, 15, 17, 21, 24, 29, 33, 36};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 15) return steps; if (a[mid] < 15) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

